    <statement><p>Use difference quotients with <m>\Delta x = 0.1</m> and
<m>\Delta y = 0.1</m> to estimate <m>f_x(4,2)</m> and
<m>f_y(4,2)</m> where
<me>f(x,y) = e^{-x}\sin\mathopen{}\left(y\right).</me></p>
<p><m>f_x(4,2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>f_y(4,2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>Then give better estimates by using <m>\Delta x = 0.01</m> and
<m>\Delta y = 0.01</m>.</p>
<p><m>f_x(4,2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>f_y(4,2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.0158487</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.00844132</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.0165714</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.00770514</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\Delta x=0.1</m> and <m>\Delta y =0.1</m>, we have the estimates:
<me>f_x(4,2) \approx \frac{f(4.1,2) - f(4,2)}{0.1}
         = \frac{e^{-4.1}\,\sin(2) - e^{-4}\,\sin(2)}{0.1}
         \approx \frac{0.0150695 - 0.0166544}{0.1} = -0.0158487.</me>
and
<me>f_y(4,2) \approx \frac{f(4,2.1) - f(4,2)}{0.1}
	= \frac{e^{-4}\,\sin(2.1) - e^{-4}\,\sin(2)}{0.1}
        \approx \frac{0.0158102 - 0.0166544}{0.1} = -0.00844132.</me>
Now, using <m>\Delta x=0.01</m> and <m>\Delta y=0.01</m>, we have the estimates:
<me>f_x(4,2) \approx \frac{f(4.01,2) - f(4,2)}{0.01}
        = \frac{e^{-4.01}\,\sin(2) - e^{-4}\,\sin(2)}{0.01}
        \approx \frac{0.0164886 - 0.0166544}{0.01} = -0.0165714</me>
and
<me>f_x(4,2) \approx \frac{f(4,2.01) - f(4,2)}{0.01}
        = \frac{e^{-4}\,\sin(2.01) - e^{-4}\,\sin(2)}{0.01}
        \approx \frac{0.0165773 - 0.0166544}{0.01} = -0.00770514.</me>



</solution>
